sortArrayWith(comparator) -> receiver or signal:
    Snapshot the receiver's elements under a read lock.
    Stable-sort a separate copy by calling the comparator without holding a lock.
    Comparator errors propagate without installing a partial ordering.
    Under a write lock, require the receiver still matches its original snapshot
    before replacing its contents with the sorted copy. Otherwise signal that the
    array changed, preserving those changes. Return the receiver on success.
